# Simple English for teaching (mandatory)

Joee's audience watches on **YouTube**. Every label, step name, caption, and body line must use **plain simple English** — not academic, engineer-only, or insider wording.

**If a viewer would need to pause and Google a word, simplify it.**

## Default rule

- **Short words** over long ones: "remove duplicates" not "deduplication"
- **Say what happens** in everyday language: "bot saves the page" not "WARC archive ingestion"
- **One idea per line** — cut filler and nested clauses
- **Prefer verbs** viewers can picture: crawl, strip, score, drop, split, train

## Banned on slides (replace or explain)

| Avoid | Use instead |
|---|---|
| deduplication | remove duplicates |
| WARC / payload / ingestion | saved copy / saved file |
| classifier (alone) | quality checker / score pages |
| positive/negative examples | good examples / bad examples |
| undersampled / oversampled | seen less often / seen more often |
| tokenization (if avoidable) | split into tokens — OK when teaching tokens |
| MinHash / fuzzy dedup | page fingerprint / near-duplicate check |
| Shift +1 / autoregressive (alone) | each token predicts the next one |
| corpus / augment / curated (alone) | dataset / add / hand-picked good sources |

Technical terms (**token**, **batch**, **loss**, **weights**) are fine when they are the lesson — not as filler.

## Accuracy still applies

Simple ≠ wrong. Follow `.cursor/rules/content-accuracy-all-topics.mdc` — **`web_search` before writing**, cite sources, flag uncertainty. When the paper uses a precise term, teach the **idea** in simple words (e.g. "quality checker trained on good web pages and books").

## Pedagogical shorthand

Labels like "self-published books" or "published books" are allowed when tagged `pedagogical` in `data/facts/*.ts` — keep them **short and plain**.

## When editing

1. Read every user-visible string aloud as if presenting to a beginner.
2. Replace jargon before shrinking font or removing rows.
3. Fix **all** labels on the same slide together — summary, tabs, footer, diagram text.

## Cross-rule dependencies

- **Legibility** (`.cursor/rules/session-video-legibility.mdc`) — large type + **short simple copy**
- **Accuracy** (`.cursor/rules/content-accuracy-all-topics.mdc`, `session-educational-accuracy.mdc`) — simple words, correct mechanisms
